/**
 * PROSTATE CANCER, hand-written trials: localised disease (monitoring against surgery against radiotherapy, the
 * fractionation trials, the brachytherapy boost, protons, tissue-preserving therapy) and locally advanced disease
 * (radiotherapy with androgen deprivation, how long that deprivation should last, and what to do after surgery).
 *
 * Every figure is quoted from the primary publication named in the record, read through Europe PMC on 25 September
 * 2026. Records that already exist in the corpus are extended by supplement in ./prostate-treatment.ts and are not
 * rewritten here: ProtecT (`protect`), CHHiP (`chhip`), PACE-B (`pace-b`), HYPO-RT-PC (`hypo-rt-pc`), PARTIQoL
 * (`partiqol`), RTOG 9601 (`rtog-9601`), POP-RT (`pop-rt`), and the registry records for NCIC PR.3/MRC PR07
 * (`nct00002633`), SPPORT (`nct00567580`) and the padeliporfin trial PCM301 (`nct01310894`).
 *
 * The thread running through this file is the one a man actually faces at diagnosis: for disease found by a PSA test,
 * the choice of treatment barely changes whether he dies of prostate cancer, and changes a great deal whether he will
 * be continent and potent afterwards. ProtecT measured both sides of that trade-off in the same men, and its
 * patient-reported outcomes are recorded here alongside its mortality figures because quoting one without the other
 * is how men end up being treated for a cancer that was never going to harm them.
 */
